# Production build config (committed — contains no secrets).
#
# VITE_API_URL is deliberately EMPTY, meaning "the API is same-origin". Firebase
# Hosting rewrites /v1/** and /health to the Cloud Run service (see
# firebase.json), so production never does a cross-origin fetch and there is no
# CORS preflight to get wrong.
#
# This file exists mainly to *override* .env.local, which Vite also loads in
# production builds. .env.local points VITE_API_URL at http://localhost:8080 for
# local dev; without this override a deploy would ship a bundle that calls the
# developer's laptop, and sign-in would fail for every real user.
#
# The VITE_FIREBASE_* web config is public by design and stays in the gitignored
# .env.local, so deploys still require that file to be present.
VITE_API_URL=
